<title>GERMANY: Prodi says Italy favours independent Euro bank.</title>
<headline>Prodi says Italy favours independent Euro bank.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Monday that Italy was clearly in favour of the future European Central Bank being independent of political control.</p>
<p>&quot;I should like to stress Italy unequivocally favours the independence of the future European central bank,&quot; he told reporters after a briefing in Frankfurt. ((  --Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525))</p>
</text>
